KG42.register("source_edge_archive-2025438a2491efe6b46080d1",{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::E::v141-c-R008-E001","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","rule_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R008-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-E-19"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008-C002"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-623d45f464e9bce4","target":"COMP-dddaa2edb4acd670","source_occurrence_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::V::coordination.local_operator","target_occurrence_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::V::settlement.payment","source_unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","target_unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Allocation of individual service-fee shares among participating PV prosumers. | Payment balance within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. | Service fees charged to participating PV prosumers for energy sharing. | Setting the service-fee level for the energy-sharing zone. | The ESP's aggregate service fee for PV energy sharing within the microgrid. | The monetary electricity-cost or income component of a PV prosumer's net energy exchange at time slot h.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g02-E-19","v141-b-g02-E-20","v141-b-g02-E-39"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"c5ecf7798c148781abe61290029ab2ac5ede47f7bc7f92239c14429f04c55928","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Information, allocation, governance or payment coordination in this mechanism: ESP computes internal buying/selling prices from supply-demand ratio and grid tariffs; prosumers iteratively reschedule; preserve service-fee and balance conditions.","target_definition":"Monetary obligations, transfers, sharing or settlement conditions in this mechanism: ESP computes internal buying/selling prices from supply-demand ratio and grid tariffs; prosumers iteratively reschedule; preserve service-fee and balance conditions.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The ESP is responsible for assuring payment balance in the energy-sharing zone. Scope: Payment balance within the microgrid energy-sharing zone.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The ESP is responsible for charging participating prosumers a service fee for energy sharing. Scope: Service fees charged to participating PV prosumers for energy sharing.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-E-19"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e03","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":"3571","section":"II. ENERGY SHARING STRUCTURE OF PV PROSUMERS / B. Energy Sharing Structure","anchor_text":"NSE FOR MICROGRIDS OF PEER-TO-PEER PROSUMERS 3571 In order to facilitate the organization of energy ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In order to facilitate the organization of energy sharing, a coordinator is required. Here, we introduce a new entity named Energy Sharing Provider (ESP). Generally, the ESP may belong to the microgrid operator or an independent third party company that focuses on the business mode of energy sharing, which provides energy sharing service for all participated PV prosumers. The ESP acts as an agent for prosumers and is responsible for assuring the power balance and the payment balance in the energy sharing zone. In this regard, the ESP is in charge of purchasing electricity from the utility grid, or from the PV prosumers with extra net power export, then selling electricity to other prosumers or the utility grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":"3571","section":"II. ENERGY SHARING STRUCTURE OF PV PROSUMERS / B. Energy Sharing Structure","anchor_text":"charge of purchasing electricity from the utility grid, or from the PV prosumers with extra net powe","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In the energy sharing zone, self-consumption of PV energy is still the first choice for PV prosumers. If PV energy can not satisfy the load demand, the PV prosumer would purchase energy agented by the ESP. If the demand of the PV prosumer is less than the production of PV source, the redundant PV power will be shared with other PV prosumers or sold to the utility grid via the ESP. In order to keep the fairness of energy sharing, the ESP should not have an optimal objective with any tendency, but it still needs to charge for service fee with the prosumers, as to cover the power losses and other possible expenditures."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-19","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"D. Income Model of the ESP","anchor_text":"tr ri D. Income Model of the ESP pr As the agent of PV energy sharing, the ESP could charge the w se","equation_id":"(20)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"As the agent of PV energy sharing, the ESP could charge the service fee from the participating prosumers, which is directly proportional to the amount of shared PV energy. The income of the ESP in an operation day is deﬁned:\nS = \\beta \\sum_{h=1}^{H} \\min \\left( TSP^{h}, TBP^{h} \\right) \\quad (20)\nwhere \\beta is the charged percentage of shared energy."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Allocation of individual service-fee shares among participating PV prosumers. | Payment balance within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. | Service fees charged to participating PV prosumers for energy sharing. | Setting the service-fee level for the energy-sharing zone. | The ESP's aggregate service fee for PV energy sharing within the microgrid. | The monetary electricity-cost or income component of a PV prosumer's net energy exchange at time slot h.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g02-E-19","v141-b-g02-E-20","v141-b-g02-E-39"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R008-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-E-19"]},"paper_scope_note":"Retain the positive and negative net-power branches, ESP organizational responsibilities, cost valuation, and the shared service fee sub-item; the iterative price, final price, and grid trading after failure cannot be treated as identical."}});
